 r←request GetCanonicalLink packageID;baseURL;target
⍝ Returns the <link rel="canonical"> tag for a "details" page, ready to be handed to
⍝ `HtmlHeader` as ⍵, or '' when the base URL cannot be established.
⍝ Every release of a major version line has a "details" page of its own, and to a search
⍝ engine they look like near-duplicates of one another - which is why so many of them end up
⍝ as "Crawled, currently not indexed". This says which page counts instead: the "versions"
⍝ page for that major line, the one that carries the README.
⍝ Nothing is hidden by it. The "details" pages stay reachable and stay linked; the tag only
⍝ says which of a set of near-identical pages should be the one that is indexed.
⍝ `Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch` copes with all the shapes a "details" page is asked for - a full
⍝ package ID, one with just a major number, one with major and minor - and yields the major
⍝ version line in every case.
 r←''
 :If 0<≢baseURL←GetBaseURL request
     target←baseURL,Reg.VersionOf_REST,'/packages/versions/',Reg.RemoveMinorAndPatch packageID
     r←⊂'<link rel="canonical" href="',(EscapeAttributeValue target),'">'
 :EndIf
